==German==

===Etymology===
Cognate to {{cog|nl|oma}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈoːma/}} {{a|standard}}
* {{IPA|de|/ˈɔma/}} {{a|chiefly western German}}
* {{audio|de|De-Oma.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f,s.gen:-:s[prenominal without an article]}}

# [[grandma]], [[granny]], [[nan]]
# any [[elderly]] [[woman]]

====Usage notes====
* The word is commonly used with a definite article in most parts of central Germany, southern Germany, and Austria: ''Wo ist die Oma?'' – “Where is Grandma?” In northern Germany—and generally in writing—no article tends to be used: ''Wo ist Oma?''

